      "summary": ": Cardrona is closed today, Friday 4 September, following significant rain overnight and high winds. The resort reports 2cm of snow overnight and in the last 24 hours, with 53cm in the past 7 days and a 108cm natural snow base at 1800m. Current mountain weather is -3°C with 58km/h winds and gusts to 114km/h; winds are forecast to increase to gale force over the next couple of hours, while snow is forecast later today. Conditions should improve as the system moves through, with lighter winds and snow showers forecast into Sunday. (Issued: 4 Sep) All in-piste skiing is closed: Kindy Conveyor, Learner Conveyors, McDougall’s Chondola, Whitestar Express, Valley View, Captains Express, T-Bar, Soho Express, Willow’s Quad and Wells Pipe Platter are closed. All listed terrain is closed, including Learners Slope, McDougall's, Whitestar, Captains, Soho, Willows, Ski Touring Access, Mt Cardrona, Arcadia Chutes and Summit. All terrain parks are also closed, including Baby Bucks, Little Bucks, Antlers Alley, Stag Lane, Big Bucks, Peoples Pipe, Olympic Pipe, Big Air and Gravity Cross. (Issued: 4 Sep) The access road is chain free, but chains must be carried, with an active road-hazard advisory. All six carparks are closed today. Masters Racing has been postponed until Saturday, 5 September, and the resort says it expects to see skiers back tomorrow.",
